! Editing and publishing

!! Local editing

From the repository root, install dependencies with `npm ci`, then run `npm run notebook:serve`. Open http://127.0.0.1:8080/ to create and edit study-note tiddlers. The server is bound to localhost.

Hand-authored notes are saved in `notebook/tiddlers/`. Commit those files to preserve and share your notes. Stop the server before rebuilding or regenerating imported content.

!! Imported project content

Run `npm run notebook:import` to refresh the guides and code. The generated bundle is `notebook/tiddlers/generated-project.json`; it is ignored by Git and rebuilt from repository files.

Edit imported guides and source in their original repository files, not in the wiki editor: imported tiddler edits are overwritten by the next import. Use new, uniquely titled tiddlers for annotations, and tag them ''Study Note''.

!! Static publishing

Run `npm run notebook:build` to create `dist/index.html`, a self-contained TiddlyWiki publication. The GitHub Actions workflow builds and deploys this file to GitHub Pages.

In the repository's Settings -> Pages, select ''GitHub Actions'' as the build source. Push your changes to the default branch, or run the workflow manually. The Pages URL is shown by the deployment workflow.

No repository token is embedded in the notebook. Editing the Pages copy does not write back to GitHub; use the local editor or repository commits for persistent updates.

!! Navigation

Imported tiddler titles are their repository-relative paths. Relative links between imported Markdown documents are converted into notebook links. Section fragments open the containing tiddler rather than scrolling to a particular heading. Links to files that are not imported and external websites are left unchanged.
